before:
Complete local Go example; the app itself does not execute it:
```go
package main
import ("fmt"; "example.test/math")
func main() { fmt.Println(math.Double(6)) }
```

after:
Keep the shown file names and folders. From the main folder, `go run .` builds this one example with the supplied local module.
```go
// File: go.mod
module example.test/app
go 1.27.0
require example.test/math v0.0.0
replace example.test/math => ./localmath

// File: localmath/go.mod
module example.test/math
go 1.27.0

// File: localmath/math.go
package math
func Double(n int) int { return n * 2 }

// File: main.go
package main
import ("fmt"; "example.test/math")
func main() { fmt.Println(math.Double(6)) }
```
